     jjooiinn reads _f_i_l_e_1 and _f_i_l_e_2, each a text file holding one
     record per line, and writes to the standard output a line
     for every pair of records, one from each file, whose _k_e_y
     fields compare equal, followed (unless -aa is given) by
     nothing else.  Either file name may be -, meaning the stan-
     dard input; both may not be - at once.

     Each input file must already be sorted on its key field, for
     example with ssoorrtt, using the same field and collating order
     as jjooiinn. By default fields are separated by runs of blanks
     and tabs, which are also stripped from the front of each
     field; with -tt every occurrence of the single separator
     character delimits a field, so empty fields are possible.
     By default the key field of each file is field 1.

